        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">A Woodway is the most durable treadmill most people will ever
          stand on, and for most home buyers it is more machine than they need.</strong> The 4Front,
          from $13,995 when we checked, makes sense for daily heavy use, heavier users and anyone
          planning on decades of ownership; the Curve LTG is the affordable way into the brand for a
          runner who wants a curved manual treadmill.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Before ordering, confirm the electrical supply, the floor, the room temperature and the
          delivery route, and read the warranty for what it is: commercial-grade terms for the
          original owner, dependent on maintenance records. If ordinary home use is the plan, our
          <a href="/landice-treadmills/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">Landice guide</a>
          and <a href="/commercial-treadmills/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">commercial-grade roundup</a>
